{
    "background_story": "Adele was the eldest child of a single mother who worked multiple jobs to make ends meet. From a young age, Adele took on a caretaking role, helping to raise her younger siblings and manage the household. As her mother's health began to decline, Adele became her primary caregiver, sacrificing her own education and career aspirations to ensure her mother's well-being. Despite the challenges, Adele's filial devotion never wavered. She nursed her mother back to health, cooked her favorite meals, and kept her company through the long nights. When her mother finally recovered, Adele's selflessness and dedication inspired her to pursue her own dreams, and she went on to become a successful social worker, helping other families in need. Adele's story is a testament to the power of filial love and the rewards of putting family first.",
